# The paths that wait for the owner's review (docs/iphone.md 12.3, #668).
#
# With branch protection on main requiring the code owner's review, GitHub merges no pull request that touches one of
# these until the owner has approved it. scripts/auto-merge refuses such a pull request too, reading this file as it is
# on main and as it is in the pull request, so that a pull request cannot take a line out and be merged by an agent.
#
# An issue that adds a file to one of these paths, or a path of the same kind (the iPhone app's entitlements, signing
# and upload configuration, P14), adds its line here in the same pull request, which the owner then reviews (12.1).
# GitHub reads the last line that matches a file, so keep every line naming the owner: a line with no owner after
# a broader one takes the file out, and scripts/auto-merge refuses everything while such a line is here. Keep the
# patterns plain too (letters, digits, . _ - /, * within a name, ** as a whole one), which is all the script reads.

# The guard itself: this file, the script that refuses, its test, and every workflow (relay.yml and iphone.yml among
# them), since any workflow can be changed to use a protected environment, and one run from main can use it once the
# owner approves the run.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @KellamA
/.github/workflows/ @KellamA
/scripts/auto-merge @KellamA
/scripts/test-auto-merge @KellamA

# The owner's own instructions for the settings that guard all this: an edit cannot change a setting, but it can mislead
# the person following them.
/docs/relay.md @KellamA

# What decides who is the person: the relay, the channel and sealing, the helper, the devices in the engine, the
